gin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">10.5k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":10530,\"repo\":\"EthicalML/awesome-production-machine-learning\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->, by the way!</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Risks</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://www.kdnuggets.com/2015/01/high-cost-machine-learning-technical-debt.html\">The High Cost of Maintaining Machine Learning Systems</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Risks</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://hunch.net/?p=22\">11 Clever Methods of Overfitting and How to Avoid Them</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Risks</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://cdt.info/ddtool/\">\"So, you want to build an ethical algorithm?\" An interactive tool to prompt discussions</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/numfocus/algorithm-ethics\">(source)</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/numfocus/algorithm-ethics\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">51</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":51,\"repo\":\"numfocus/algorithm-ethics\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Deep Learning</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><strong><a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=mG4imMEAAAAJ&#x26;hl=en\">Prof. Andrew Ng's</a> <a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/specializations/deep-learning\">courses on Deep Learning</a>!</strong> There five courses, as part of the <a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/specializations/deep-learning\">Deep Learning Specialization on Coursera</a>. These courses are part of his new venture, <a href=\"https://www.deeplearning.ai\">deeplearning.ai</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Deep Learning</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.deeplearningbook.org/\"><em>Deep Learning</em></a>, a free book published MIT Press.</strong> By Ian Goodfellow, Yoshua Bengio and Aaron Courville</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Big data</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.kdnuggets.com/2015/02/10-things-statistics-big-data-analysis.html\">10 things statistics taught us about big data analysis</a> (and some more food for thought: <a href=\"https://www.datasciencecentral.com/profiles/blogs/what-statisticians-think-about-data-scientists\">\"What Statisticians think about Data Scientists\"</a>)</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Big data</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.thetalkingmachines.com/episodes/economic-impact-machine-learning-and-using-kernel-trick-big-data\">\"Talking Machines\" #12</a>: Interviews Prof. Andrew Ng (from <a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/machine-learning\">his course, which has its own module on big data</a>); this episode covers some problems relevant to <em>high-dimensional</em> data</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Big data</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.thetalkingmachines.com/episodes/really-really-big-data-and-machine-learning-business\">\"Talking Machines\" #15: \"Really Really Big Data and Machine Learning in Business\"</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Big data</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/0xnr/awesome-bigdata\">0xnr/awesome-bigdata</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/0xnr/awesome-bigdata\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">10.5k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":10490,\"repo\":\"0xnr/awesome-bigdata\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More Data Science materials</h2><h3>Aside: Bayesian Statistics and Machine Learning</h3>","itemHTML":"<li>The <strong>free book</strong> <em><a href=\"http://camdavidsonpilon.github.io/Probabilistic-Programming-and-Bayesian-Methods-for-Hackers/\">Probabilistic Programming and Bayesian Methods for Hackers</a></em>. Made with a \"computation/understanding-first, mathematics-second point of view.\" Uses <a href=\"https://github.com/pymc-devs/pymc\">PyMC</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/pymc-devs/pymc\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">6.2k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":6220,\"repo\":\"pymc-devs/pymc\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->. It's available in print too!</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More Data Science materials</h2><h3>Aside: Bayesian Statistics and Machine Learning</h3>","itemHTML":"<li>Like learning by playing? Me too. Try <a href=\"https://github.com/fulldecent/19-questions\">19 Questions</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/fulldecent/19-questions\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">15</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":15,\"repo\":\"fulldecent/19-questions\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->, \"a machine learning game which asks you questions and guesses an object you are thinking about,\" and <strong>explains which Bayesian statistics techniques it's using!</strong></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More Data Science materials</h2><h3>Aside: Bayesian Statistics and Machine Learning</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.manning.com/liveprojectseries/time-series-forecasting-with-bayesian-modeling\"><em>Time Series Forecasting with Bayesian Modeling by Michael Grogan</em></a>, a 5-project series - paid but the first project is free.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More Data Science materials</h2><h3>Aside: Bayesian Statistics and Machine Learning</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/markdregan/Bayesian-Modelling-in-Python\">Bayesian Modelling in Python</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/markdregan/Bayesian-Modelling-in-Python\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">2.3k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":2332,\"repo\":\"markdregan/Bayesian-Modelling-in-Python\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->. Uses <a href=\"https://github.com/pymc-devs/pymc\">PyMC</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/pymc-devs/pymc\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">6.2k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":6220,\"repo\":\"pymc-devs/pymc\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> as well.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T23:07:10.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"APA-Technology-Division/urban-and-regional-planning-resources","categoryHTML":"<h2>Educational and Informational Resources</h2><h3>Literature Resources</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://law.unc.edu/academics/centers-and-programs/ai-dr-program/clearinghouse/\">Automated Decision-Making and the Law Clearinghouse Project</a> - The aim of this clearinghouse project thus is to highlight seminal and impactful articles focused on issues of AI Decision-Making and the law.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-02T22:56:14.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"analysis-tools-dev/static-analysis","categoryHTML":"<h2>Other</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/angular-eslint/angular-eslint#readme\">Angular ESLint</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/angular-eslint/angular-eslint#readme\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">1.1k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":1098,\"repo\":\"angular-eslint/angular-eslint\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - Linter for Angular projects</li>","updatedAt":